+# Incidents brief, August–September 2026
+
+"Open": the meeting notes do not record it as done.
+
+## 11 August: ingest stall, full disk
+
+- **Impact:** Customer dashboards stale for about 2.5 hours overnight; no data lost.
+- **Cause:** One malformed batch jammed ingest; endless retries filled the database disk with logs.
+- **Fix:** Restarted ingest, setting the bad batch aside; freed disk space.
+- **Follow-ups:**
+  - Disk alert at 80%: no owner named; open (disk hit 85% again in September, caught by hand).
+  - Fix so bad batches cannot jam ingest: Jonas; open.
+  - Paging escalation rules: Elif and Sunil; done, confirmed 30 September.
+  - Handbook check for old wait time: Mara; open.
+
+## 21 September: API certificate expiry
+
+- **Impact:** Public API unreachable for 47 minutes; nearly all customers failed to connect.
+- **Cause:** Certificate expired; its automatic renewal had silently failed all month after a credential change.
+- **Fix:** Renewed certificate, restarted API; renewal job repaired and now alerts on failure (done).
+- **Follow-ups (no owners named):**
+  - Reminder 14 days before each expiry: open.
+  - Alert on days left: open.
+  - Expiry check in weekly checklist: open.
+  - Incident handlers record steps as they work: agreed practice.
